# M5.3 acceptance: reader context, the context chip and "Ask about selection",
# against the logging fake sidecar tests/acceptance/m5.3-fake-sidecar.py.
# Run it through tests/acceptance/m5.3.sh, which builds the fixture under
# /tmp/agentic-reader-m5.3 and writes what each
# `run /tmp/agentic-reader-m5.3/promptcheck <n> <name>` compares prompt n with
# (text and context, exactly). The session is
#   scripts/shot.sh -o <out> -s tests/acceptance/m5.3.steps -- \
#     env HOME=/tmp/agentic-reader-m5.3/home \
#       READER_SIDECAR_CMD=$PWD/tests/acceptance/m5.3-fake-sidecar.py \
#       READER_FAKE_LOG=/tmp/agentic-reader-m5.3/prompts.log \
#       ./build/app/agentic-reader /tmp/agentic-reader-m5.3/proj/attention.pdf
#
# The fake answers each prompt at once with "Fake reply to prompt <n>,
# context: file attention.pdf, page 3, page_count 4, selection of 469 chars."
# (or "... no selection.", or "no context."), which the shots can be read by.
#
# Interface choices where the spec is silent (see also tests/test_reader_context.cpp):
#   - The chip text is "<file name> · p. <1-based current page> · <n> chars
#     selected" ("1 char selected"; no third part without a selection or after
#     the x). n counts Unicode code points. With no PDF open there is no chip.
#   - The x on the chip shows while the chip includes a selection. It leaves the
#     selection out of the next prompt only; the chip drops its third part
#     until that prompt is sent and shows it again afterwards (while the PDF
#     selection still exists).
#   - The PDF context menu gets "&Ask about selection" after "Copy" (it may
#     show "Ctrl+Shift+A"), enabled only with a selection. The steps pick it by
#     its mnemonic: `key a` while the menu is open.
#   - Ctrl+Shift+A works while the PDF view has the focus (a frame accelerator
#     or a menu item, the implementer's choice). Without a selection it does
#     nothing.
#   - "Ask about selection" replaces the empty input with the pre-fill, puts the
#     caret at its end (after the blank line) and focuses the input, so typing
#     continues after the quote.
#
# Layout these coordinates assume (1400x900 window at the screen origin, no
# window manager, measured on the M5.2 build): PDF pane x 225..980; at fit
# width ("119%") a page whose top edge is at the top of the pane spans x
# 237..967 from y 79, and a point (x, y) in page points is at
# (237 + 1.1944 x, 79 + 1.1944 y). Page 3's paragraph runs from "Scaled" at
# (343, 209) to "omega." at (709, 310); "regions" is at (686, 259); (600, 600)
# is empty page space. The chat pane is x 990..1395: message view from y 72,
# input y 775..833 (click it at (1180, 800)), Send and Stop y 840..872. The
# chip is one row between the message view and the input, at most 32 px tall,
# its bottom edge within 8 px of the input's top edge, and its x is the
# rightmost item of that row, at least 16 px wide, its right edge within 12 px
# of the input's right edge (x 1395). So a click at (1380, 757) hits the x.
wait 3

# Start. Page 1 of attention.pdf at fit width ("119%", entry "1 / 4"). The chat
# pane shows an empty message view and the input with Send and Stop, no
# first-run banner. Directly above the input the chip reads
# "attention.pdf · p. 1" and nothing more (no selection, no x).
shot start

click 600 600
key ctrl+g
key ctrl+a
type 3
key Return
wait 2

# Page 3 ("Page 3" heading and its 7-line paragraph) fills the PDF pane, entry
# "3 / 4". The chip now reads "attention.pdf · p. 3". Nothing is highlighted.
shot page-3

drag 343 209 709 310
wait 1

# The whole paragraph is highlighted, "Scaled" to "omega.", the heading is not.
# The chip reads "attention.pdf · p. 3 · 469 chars selected" with an x at its
# right end. The input is still empty.
shot selected

key ctrl+shift+a
wait 1

# Ctrl+Shift+A: the input has the keyboard focus (caret visible) and holds the
# pre-fill: lines starting with "> ", the quoted first 300 chars of the
# paragraph, whose last quoted line is "> with very small gradients. Mult" (cut
# mid-word), then an empty line where the caret sits. The input may be
# scrolled to show only the last lines. The highlight and the chip are
# unchanged.
shot ask-shortcut-prefill

type what does this mean?
wait 0.5

# Typing went into the input after the blank line: its last lines are
# "> with very small gradients. Mult", an empty line, "what does this mean?".
shot ask-shortcut-typed

key Return
wait 2
run /tmp/agentic-reader-m5.3/promptcheck 1 ask-shortcut

# Sent. The message view shows the user message (the quote, which may render
# as plain "> " lines, then "what does this mean?") and the reply "Fake reply
# to prompt 1, context: file attention.pdf, page 3, page_count 4, selection of
# 469 chars." The input is empty. The paragraph is still highlighted and the
# chip still reads "attention.pdf · p. 3 · 469 chars selected".
shot ask-shortcut-sent

click 686 259 3
wait 1

# Right-click on "regions" inside the selection: a popup menu at the pointer
# with "Copy" and, below it, "Ask about selection" (enabled, black text; it may
# show "Ctrl+Shift+A"). The highlight is unchanged where the menu does not
# cover it.
shot context-menu

key a
wait 1

# "Ask about selection" from the menu: the menu is gone, the input has the
# focus and holds the same pre-fill as before, ending with the empty line.
shot ask-menu-prefill

type and the last line?
key Return
wait 2
run /tmp/agentic-reader-m5.3/promptcheck 2 ask-menu

click 1380 757
wait 1

# The x on the chip: the chip reads "attention.pdf · p. 3" (no "chars
# selected", no x). The paragraph in the PDF is still highlighted.
shot chip-excluded

click 1180 800
type Summarize this page.
key Return
wait 2
run /tmp/agentic-reader-m5.3/promptcheck 3 excluded

# The excluded prompt went without the selection: the newest reply reads "Fake
# reply to prompt 3, context: file attention.pdf, page 3, page_count 4, no
# selection." Since that prompt is sent, the chip reads "attention.pdf · p. 3 ·
# 469 chars selected" again, with its x. The paragraph is still highlighted.
shot excluded-sent

click 1180 800
type And now?
key Return
wait 2
run /tmp/agentic-reader-m5.3/promptcheck 4 included-again

# The next prompt carries the selection again: the newest reply reads "Fake
# reply to prompt 4, context: file attention.pdf, page 3, page_count 4,
# selection of 469 chars."
shot included-again

click 600 600
wait 1
click 600 600 3
wait 1

# No selection: nothing is highlighted, the chip reads "attention.pdf · p. 3".
# The right-click menu shows "Copy" and "Ask about selection", both greyed out.
shot context-menu-disabled

key Escape
wait 1
key ctrl+shift+a
wait 1

# Ctrl+Shift+A without a selection did nothing: the menu is gone and the input
# is empty. The chat view still ends with the reply to prompt 4.
shot shortcut-without-selection

key ctrl+shift+o
wait 2
key alt+Home
wait 1
key ctrl+l
wait 1
key space
key Home
run xdotool type --delay 0 /tmp/agentic-reader-m5.3/empty
key End BackSpace
wait 1
key Return
wait 3

# Open Project on the empty folder closed the PDF: the PDF pane is empty, the
# project header names "empty", the entry shows no page. There is no chip
# above the input (the message view reaches down to the input or a blank row
# sits there, with no text in it).
shot no-pdf

click 1180 800
type Is a file open?
key Return
wait 2
run /tmp/agentic-reader-m5.3/promptcheck 5 no-pdf

# The prompt went without context: the newest reply reads "Fake reply to
# prompt 5, no context." Still no chip.
shot no-pdf-sent
